WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.537
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Strengths Spotlight.

00:00:12.537 --> 00:00:17.074
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:17.074 --> 00:00:19.796
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:19.796 --> 00:00:22.518
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:22.518 --> 00:00:30.684
Every person has things they do well. Grown-ups call them strengths.

00:00:30.684 --> 00:00:38.851
A strength can be loud, like running fast. Or quiet, like being patient, or kind.

00:00:38.851 --> 00:00:44.295
Today we turn on a soft spotlight, and let it rest on one of yours — not the best one, just one that is true.

00:00:44.295 --> 00:00:47.924
You can do this with eyes closed, or eyes open, looking softly at your desk.

00:00:47.924 --> 00:00:56.998
Think back over your day, slowly, like turning pages in a book.

00:00:56.998 --> 00:01:03.350
Was there a moment you tried again, even when it was hard? That is a strength: trying again.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:11.516
Was there a moment you were kind, or patient, or a good listener? Those are strengths, too.

00:01:11.516 --> 00:01:20.590
Quiet strengths count. They are real, and they are yours.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:30.571
Now pick one strength you used today. Just one, just for now.

00:01:30.571 --> 00:01:36.015
Say its name in your mind: I was patient. I kept trying. I was kind.

00:01:36.015 --> 00:01:42.367
Picture the soft spotlight resting on it. It does not need to shine for anyone else.

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:47.811
It only needs to be seen by you. That is enough.

00:01:47.811 --> 00:01:54.162
Your strength stays with you. It goes where you go, all day long.

00:01:54.162 --> 00:02:01.421
That is Strengths Spotlight. Noticing one true strength, and letting it be seen.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:04.143
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:04.143 --> 00:02:07.773
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:07.773 --> 00:02:11.402
You're ready for what's next.
